<title>USA: Pahaquarry Township, N.J., merges with Hardwick.</title>
<headline>Pahaquarry Township, N.J., merges with Hardwick.</headline>
<dateline>PAHAQUARRY, N.J. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The tiny New Jersey township of Pahaquarry disappeared Tuesday, State News service reported.</p>
<p>The town, much of which lies inside the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area, fell below the population level needed to sustain municipal status and merged into neighboring Hardwick.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
